{
  "id": "singular-plural",
  "title": "Singular & Plural",
  "lesson": {
    "intro": "[[Singular]] means one. [[Plural]] means more than one.",
    "points": [
      "Most nouns add -s: cat → [[cats]], book → [[books]].",
      "Nouns ending in s, x, sh, ch add -es: bus → [[buses]], box → [[boxes]], brush → [[brushes]], watch → [[watches]].",
      "Some nouns ending in o add -es: tomato → [[tomatoes]], potato → [[potatoes]].",
      "Consonant + y → change y to i and add -es: baby → [[babies]]. Vowel + y → just add -s: toy → [[toys]].",
      "Many nouns ending in f or fe change to -ves: leaf → [[leaves]], knife → [[knives]].",
      "Irregular plurals: child → [[children]], man → [[men]], woman → [[women]], tooth → [[teeth]], foot → [[feet]], mouse → [[mice]].",
      "Some nouns stay the same: one [[sheep]], two sheep; one [[fish]], many fish; one [[deer]], three deer."
    ],
    "examples": [
      {
        "text": "one apple → two [[apples]]",
        "note": "add -s"
      },
      {
        "text": "one box → three [[boxes]]",
        "note": "add -es"
      },
      {
        "text": "one butterfly → many [[butterflies]]",
        "note": "y → ies"
      },
      {
        "text": "one leaf → many [[leaves]]",
        "note": "f → ves"
      },
      {
        "text": "one child → five [[children]]",
        "note": "irregular"
      }
    ],
    "tip": "Say the plural out loud. If you hear an extra \"iz\" sound (boxes, buses), you probably need -es."
  },
